<title>CYPRUS: Arab Super Light exports delayed in Oct - MEES.</title>
<headline>Arab Super Light exports delayed in Oct - MEES.</headline>
<dateline>NICOSIA 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Exports of Saudi Aramco's Arab Super Light (ASL) crude will be subject to lifting delays over a three-week period in October because of maintenance work at the Yanbu loading terminal, the Middle East Economic Survey (MEES) reported on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;The repairs are expected to be completed by the end of the month, however, after which normal deliveries of the grade will resume,&quot; the Cyprus-based weekly said.</p>
<p>ASL production runs at some 200,000 barrels per day (bpd) and is sold mostly to South Korea where Saudi Aramco has a joint venture refinery deal.</p>
</text>
